WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.868
Before the size of the job, it
helps to know which job is whose,

2
00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:07.375
because one O U tree holds
four different populations.

3
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:10.100
The workbook treats them as four tracks.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.559
People, the HR track: Book 02
builds the directory side,

5
00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:17.600
and Book 03 supplies the attributes.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.632
End-user devices and servers,
the Intune and Arc tracks:

7
00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:27.188
Book 02's Group Policy analysis finds
their settings, and Book 05 moves them.

8
00:00:27.188 --> 00:00:32.780
And the non-person track: every service
account gets an owner and a target,

9
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.763
here in Book 02, with
AI agents in Book 17.

10
00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:39.194
Appendix A maps that work
to account management,

11
00:00:39.194 --> 00:00:45.113
attribute-based access and least
privilege in NIST 800-53, and to M-22-09.

12
00:00:45.113 --> 00:00:48.000
Next, everything else
the directory holds up.
